{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Climate risk of many sites at once (portfolio table)"},"description":"A list of sites, a portfolio, addresses or spreadsheet rows screened in one call: the long-term layers of get_climate_profile at up to 200 places, as a table, a row per place and a column per layer and band. By default the headline exposures: river and coastal flood depth, sea level rise, heat, heavy rain, water stress, drought, wildfire, earthquake hazard and the climate zone; narrow it with categories (flooding...) or layer ids. Each row carries a home's damage band there.\n\nUse it whenever two or more places are asked about, rather than a profile per place: rank sites on the bands and columns, or compare places on the same layers. One place in depth: get_climate_profile.","inputSchema":{"$defs":{"PlaceGiven":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"One place, by its name or its coordinates.","properties":{"latitude":{"description":"Latitude, WGS84; or give place_name","maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"longitude":{"description":"Longitude, WGS84; or give place_name","maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"place_name":{"description":"A place name or street address; add the country after a comma when ambiguous (Portland, Maine)","type":"string"}},"type":"object"}},"properties":{"categories":{"description":"The layers of these categories; the headline exposures when neither this nor layers","items":{"enum":["temperature","precipitation","wind","water","flooding","vegetation","misc","terrain","landcover"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"language":{"default":"en","description":"Language code for the name of the place found (resolved_from); the rest of the answer is English","enum":["en","de","fr","it","es","nl","pl","uk","ro","sr","ru"],"type":"string"},"layers":{"description":"These layers, by the ids get_climate_profile takes (fetch catalog:layers)","items":{"type